From d9e083bedd101ea8bf8800b7513fe55916923336 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 15:13:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Render only animals inside a configured box, at their scale
 attribute

- bluemap-entities.properties next to the jar holds the box (block
  coordinates, bounds included). It is created with the defaults if it is
  missing and re-read on every BlueMap resource load (/bluemap reload).
- After all resource packs are loaded, a resource-pack extension drops every
  entity-state that is not an animal (passive and neutral animals, fish,
  water mobs, bats; no hostile mobs, villagers, golems, allays or props)
  and routes every remaining part through FilteredRendererType, including
  parts that use BlueMap's own default renderer.
- FilteredRendererType skips entities outside the box and scales each
  rendered part by the entity's minecraft:scale attribute, around the
  entity's feet before BlueMap rotates and places it.
- The mob entity-classes now extend LivingEntity, which reads the final
  minecraft:scale value from the saved attributes list (base, add_value,
  add_multiplied_base, add_multiplied_total, clamped to 0.0625..16) with a
  lenient field deserializer, so a malformed attribute can never drop an
  entity. Animals without an own class (bat, cod, tadpole) use it as well.
- Tests run against BlueMap's real entity deserializer and tile model.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UcEcjHB2xgUsmrFLaA4fZn
